  "notes": "Baseline seeded manually on 2026-10-21 (first state file for this contract). ath.price_usd is the true all-time high (CoinGecko, 2026-05-28), not the tracking-start price, so the ATH gate cannot false-fire until the token genuinely exceeds it. Targets pre-registered from aeon.yml var so a crossing between runs is caught rather than swallowed by the skill's first-observation rule. h1_pct is stored as null when no trade occurred in the window (DexScreener omits h1 rather than printing 0) - do not read null as 'flat'. Two distinct 'buy' shapes appear on this book and must not be conflated: a single-venue print from a fresh EOA that KEEPS the balance is directional; a same-block sweep of 4-5 pools into one hop then forwarded to a shared sink that ends at 0 balance is arb/aggregator. A third tell, cheaper than decoding receipts: the SAME sender buying in one pool and selling in another within the same second is a two-leg arb. Always balanceOf the receiver before calling an uptick accumulation - and encode balanceOf calldata as selector + 24 hex zeros + the 40-hex address (74 hex chars), never zero-pad the address on the right. FOURTH TELL, added 2026-10-23 15:05Z: a wallet whose eth_getCode starts 0xef0100 is an EIP-7702 delegated smart account - it is NOT a fresh bot EOA, so 'fresh EOA keeps balance' understates it; check the designator before classifying. Also: buy/sell COUNT is not buy/sell DOLLARS on a thin book - 4 buys vs 18 sells at 15:05Z was 74/26 in dollars because the sells were $49 MM clips and the buy was $4.3k. FIFTH TELL, added 2026-10-23 16:01Z: DexScreener priceChange.h1 sign and magnitude can be pure noise on a thin book - at 16:01Z the deepest pool read h1 -0.08% on 0 buys / 8 sells while the USDC pool read -0.12% on 6 buys / 1 sell; both are the same wallets' cross-pool arb legs mirrored, so pool-level direction is meaningless when the same sender appears on both sides."
